cuems-common (1.3.0-10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * cuems-nodeconf.service: drop RemainAfterExit=yes. cuems-nodeconf is now a
    long-running daemon (resident avahi discovery loop + interface-scoped alias
    supervision), not a one-shot. With Type=notify, RemainAfterExit=yes would
    leave the unit 'active (exited)' when the daemon dies, masking the failure
    from dependents and from Restart= monitoring. Pairs with the cuems-nodeconf
    Phase-1 re-enable.

