cuems-common (1.3.0-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Retire the legacy per-conffile dpkg-divert + .cuems mechanism for eight
    config files (it diverted several other packages' conffiles -- systemd,
    isc-dhcp-server, isc-dhcp-client, avahi, xserver -- and the .cuems copy
    sources are obsolete, so the copies were dead). postinst now migrates:
    - journald/rsyslog policy moves to drop-ins (journald.conf.d/cuems.conf,
      rsyslog.d/cuems.conf); their main conffiles are un-diverted and handed
      back to systemd/rsyslog.
    - dhclient.conf, isc-dhcp-server default, Xwrapper.config, hostapd.conf
      (unused; cuems uses /run/cuems/hostapd.conf) are un-diverted + restored
      to their owning package; cuems no longer ships them.
    - avahi-daemon.conf + dhcpd.conf have no drop-in, so they stay a divert but
      ship as /usr/share/cuems/ templates installed by postinst on FIRST
      install only (operator edits survive upgrades). The avahi template no
      longer hardcodes host-name -- avahi falls back to the OS hostname, fixing
      the cloned-node mDNS collision.
  * Stop shipping rsyslog.conf, avahi-daemon.conf, dhcpd.conf, hostapd.conf as
    conffiles.

